details:
(a) number of places where newly constructed part of National Highways and bridges have collapsed or damaged within three years after inaguration, during the last five years, year-wise;
(b) number of places where newly constructed part of National Highways and bridges have collapsed or damaged within one year after inaguration, during the last five years, year-wise;
(c) number of places where the newly constructed part of National Highways and bridges have collapsed or damaged before the completion of the work, during the last five years, year-wise; and
(e) reason and action on companies, name of company, year-wise and State-wise?

(a) the number of hospitals under the union health Ministry;
(b) the details of the capacity of these hospitals, institution-wise and year-wise during the last five years;
(c) the details of number of vacant and total posts in these hospitals, institution-wise and year-wise during that period;
(d) the details of number of permanent posts, institution-wise and year-wise during the last five years; and
(e) the details of number of contractual employees, institution-wise and year-wise during that period?

(a) the number branches of Public Sector Banks closed in last five years, bank-wise and year-wise details;
(b) the number branches of Public Sector Banks opened in last five years, bank-wise and year-wise details; 
(c) the number of employees in Public Sector Banks in last five years, bank-wise and year-wise details; and
(d) the number of account holders in Public Sector Banks in last five years, bank-wise and year-wise details?

(a) whether Government is aware of concerns expressed by economists and researchers regarding the comparability of the Periodic Labour Force Survey (PLFS) estimates with the earlier Employment–Unemployment Surveys conducted by the National Sample Survey Office (NSSO);
(b) the reasons for the methodological changes introduced in the PLFS;
(c) whether Government has undertaken any study to ensure comparability of employment data across different survey methodologies; and
(d) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the names of Central Public Sector Enterprises (CPSEs) under the Ministry that have transferred their shares during the last five years;
(b) the details of private parties that have bought the shares of each of those CPSEs;
(c) the quantity of each of those share transfers and the year of transfer; and
(d) the names of CPSEs that were taken over or whose shares were bought by State Governments and the year of transfer?

(a) the year-wise allocation and actual expenditure by Government on scientific research and development done during the last five years;
(b) what percentage of Gross Domestic Product does it constitute;
(c) Government institutions which are working for research and development;
(d) the fund allocation and expenditure, year-wise and institution-wise;
(e) the number of patents received by these institutions, institution-wise, year-wise;and
(f) the details of the amount spend on these projects by Government?

(a) the country-wise details of foreign visits undertaken by the Prime Minister since 2021;
(b) the total expenditure incurred on such visit since 2021, year-wise and visit-wise; and
(c) the country-wise details of bilateral agreements/MoUs signed during these visits, the investment commitments announced, and the actual Foreign Direct Investment (FDI) received in India as a result thereof?

(a) the existing law/policy/guidelines dealing with the modifications of vehicles;
(b) what categories of vehicle modifications are now permitted without and with prior approval from the registering authority, the details thereof;
(c) whether State Governments have the power to alter these guidelines or make their own policies regarding modifications;
(d) if so, details thereof; and
(e) if so, whether any State Government has made its own policies on vehicle modification till now, if so, the details thereof?

(a) number of bridges/overbridges/fly overs/viaducts, inspected under National Highway safety audits;
(b) bridges identified as structurally deficient along with the details of year of construction; and
(c) the details of the National Highway repairing and completing the work and timeline for completion of remaining works?

(a) the total number of cases registered by the Enforcement Directorate (ED) and Income Tax Department, the year-wise details for last five years;
(b) the Number of cases where trial has not started;
(c) the Number of undertrial prisoners currently in jail;
(d) the number of cases convicted, the year-wise details for last five years; and
(e) the number of under trial prisoners found not guilty by the court, the year-wise details for last five years?

(a) the number of women-owned manufacturing MSMEs registered during the last five years, State-wise, year-wise details;
(b) employment generated, State-wise, year-wise;
(c) financial assistance extended under Government schemes, year-wise, State-wise; and
(d) the number of these registered MSMEs closed, year-wise, State-wise?

(a) the total number of sanctioned posts of teaching and non-teaching staff in the research and educational institutions functioning under the Ministry, including institutions under the Indian Council of Agricultural Research, the details thereof, social category-wise;
(b) the number of posts lying vacant in these institutions, category-wise and institution-wise, the details thereof, social category-wise;
(c) the number of vacancies reported during each of the last five years, year-wise, the details thereof, social category-wise; and
(d) the number of recruitments made for teaching and non-teaching posts during the above period, the details thereof, social category-wise?

(a) whether Government maintains the statistics of workers in private sector in the country;
(b) if so, the details of workers in different types of private sector, year-wise and sector-wise;
(c) if not, the reasons therefor;
(d) whether Government has implemented any direct beneficiary schemes for private sector workers during the last five years;
(e) if so, the details of funds released under those schemes, State-wise and year-wise; and
(f) whether Government would provide any monetary or other type of relief to those workers who loose their jobs in layoffs?

(a) the average AQI and other pollution indicators in each quarter of last five years;
(b) whether Government was able to analyse the causes behind the high scale pollution in Delhi;
(c) the steps taken to deal with the issue;
(d) whether any noticeable progress has been achieved so far; and
(e) if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) the number of teaching post vacancies in Central Universities and Centrally Funded Technical Institutions (CFTI), institution-wise, year-wise and social category-wise, details of last five years; 
(b) the number of vacancies in PhD in Central Universities and CFTIs, institution-wise, year-wise and social category-wise, details of last five years; 
(c) number of new teaching posts created in Central Universities and CFTIs, institution-wise and year-wise, details of last five years; and 
(d) number of new seats created in PhD in Central Universities and CFTIs, institution-wise and year-wise, details of last five years?

(a) the number of operational National Waterways, the total navigable length and the year-wise funds allocated and utilised for inland water transport during the last five years; 
(b) the status of passenger and cargo movement on inland waterways, including waterway-wise and State-wise traffic volumes and the number of terminals, jetties and ferry services currently operational; and 
(c) the measures being taken to promote inland water travel, improve last-mile connectivity, ensure passenger safety and enhance affordability and environmental sustainability?

(a) the year-wise retail prices of domestic and commercial LPG cylinders during the last five years;
(b) the number of gas cylinder bookings given in 2026, month-wise and company-wise data;
(c) the number of gas cylinder bookings given in Pradhan Mantri Ujjwala Yojna (PMUY) in 2026, month-wise details thereof;
(d) whether Government has assessed the impact of LPG price rise on households and small entrepreneurs, including restaurants, tea shops etc;
(e) whether Government intend to provide any financial assistance to support small-scale entrepreneurs, if so, the details thereof; and
(f) if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) the mechanism adopted by Indian Railways for collection, treatment and disposal of waste generated from trains and railway stations;
(b) whether waste treatment plants have been established for processing such waste;
(c) if so, the number of such plants, zone-wise, along with their treatment capacities; and
(d) the designation of officers responsible for waste management at the station, divisional, zonal and Railway Board levels?

(a) the details of the funds released by the Union Government for each State under Viksit Bharat Guarantee for Rozgar and Aajeevika Mission Gramin (VB-G RAM G);
(b) the details of the funds released for each State under MGNREGA in last five years, year-wise;
(c) the details of the number of beneficiaries for each State under MGNREGA in last five years, year-wise; and
(d) the details of the number of work days ensured for each State under MGNREGA in last five years, year-wise?

(a) whether Government has any ongoing scheme to promote Football and if so, the details thereof;
(b) the details of funds allocated and utilised during the last five years;
(c) the reasons why the All India Football Federation (AIFF) has resolved to change its name to the Football Federation of Bharat (FFB); and
(d) the benefits this name change would bring to the Indian Football?

(a) whether Government is aware that in the ranking given by the World Economic Forum, Indian Passport has declined from 74th in 2013 to 80th in 2026;
(b) the reasons for the decline of Indian Passport in global rankings;
(c) whether the Indian Passport is also issued to Non- Indian Citizens; and
(d) if so, the details thereof including past precedents?
GK

(a) permanent staff strength of NTA, post-wise;
(b) contractual staff strength, post-wise;
(c) examination-wise details of all examinations conducted during the last five years;
(d) examination-wise details of re-examinations conducted during the last five years;
(e) examination-wise registration fee collected; and
(f) examination-wise expenditure incurred?

(a) funds released under PM SHRI schemeduring last five years;
(b) State-wise details thereof;
(c) whether PM SHRI schools follow NCERT syllabus, State syllabus or both; and
(d) whether Government proposes flexibility in curriculum implementation?
J

(a) whether Government maintains national data on hospital-acquired infections;
(b) the details thereof institution-wise;
(c) the measures taken for infection surveillance; and
(d) whether national guidelines are proposed in this regard?

(a) the number of complaints received regarding deceptive online interface designs;
(b) the action taken thereon;
(c) the penalties imposed on those who committed such deception; and
(d) the consumer awareness measures undertaken to protect them from dark patterns?
bs

(a) whether Government has received complaints regarding vehicle performance after introduction of E20 petrol;
(b) the number of complaints received, State-wise;
(c) whether any scientific study has been conducted regarding the compatibility of older vehicles with E20 fuel;
(d) whether Government proposes to continue supply of pure petrol (E0/E10) for vehicles not designed for E20 fuel; and
(e) if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) whether Government of Kerala had earlier objected to displaying Government symbols, logos or publicity boards in front of houses constructed under PMAY;
(b) whether the present Government of Kerala has communicated any change in its position;
(c) whether Government has issued any mandatory guidelines regarding such displays; and
(d) whether Government proposes to discontinue compulsory display of publicity material in order to uphold the dignity and self-respect of beneficiaries?

(a) whether Government is aware of the reasons of collapse of sections of the National Highways (NHs), including the incident near Kottayam in Kollam district and similar incidents reported in other places in Kerala during the construction of the National Highway 66;
(b) whether Government or the National Highways Authority of India has conducted any technical or expert study into these incidents and the findings thereof;
(c) the action taken against contractors, consultants or agencies responsible; and
(d) whether Government proposes to review the design and construction practices for highway projects in flood-prone or marshy areas of Kerala?

(a) the total number of sanctioned teaching and non-teaching posts in Central universities, and Central educational institution, along with the number of posts currently vacant, university-wise;
(b) the category-wise breakup of these vacancies for Scheduled Castes (SC), Scheduled Tribes (ST), Other Backward Classes (OBC), Economically Weaker Sections (EWS) and unreserved categories;
(c) the number of reserved posts lying vacant for SC, ST, OBC and EWS categories in these universities; and
(d) whether Government has issued any direction to Central universities to fill up these vacancies within a stipulated time frame?

(a) the total quantity of Liquefied Petroleum Gas (LPG) produced in the country during each of the last five years, year-wise;
(b) the proportion of domestic LPG production vis-à-vis total LPG consumption in the country during the same period;
(c) whether Government has undertaken or approved any new investments to increase domestic LPG production capacity in the country during the last five years; and
(d) the details of such investments, along with the amount invested and the locations of these projects?

(a) the total amount of subsidy provided by Government on domestic LPG during each of the last five years, year-wise;
(b) the scheme-wise break-up of the subsidy provided under schemes such as Direct Benefit Transfer for LPG (DBTL) and Pradhan Mantri Ujjwala Yojana (PMUY);
(c) the number of beneficiaries who received LPG subsidy under each of the above schemes during each of the last five years;
(d) the number of beneficiaries covered under each scheme, State/UT-wise; and
(e) the amount of LPG subsidy transferred to beneficiaries under each scheme during the last five years, State/UT-wise?

(a) the total number of sanctioned posts in Indian Railways and the number of posts currently lying vacant, zone-wise and category-wise;
(b) the number of recruitments made in Indian Railways during the last five years, year-wise and category-wise;
(c) number of vacancies in safety and operational categories separately; and
(d) the details of recruitment notifications issued through Railway Recruitment Boards during the last three years and the number of posts for which recruitment has been completed so far?

(a) the number of new beneficiaries added each year during the last five years, scheme-wise, for Central Sector Scheme of Scholarship for College and University Students, National Means-cum-Merit Scholarship Scheme, Prime Minister’s Special Scholarship Scheme for Jammu & Kashmir and Ladakh, Central Sector Interest Subsidy Scheme for Education Loans and PM Vidyalaxmi Education Loan Scheme;
(b) the total funds allocated, released and actually spent under each of the above schemes during the last five years, year-wise; and
(c) the amount of funds that remained unspent or lapsed, scheme-wise, during the same period?

(a) the number of goods for which GST rates were reduced during the recent GST Council decisions;
(b) the number of such goods whose market prices have actually declined thereafter;
(c) whether any post-rate-cut study or assessment has been conducted to examine the pass-through of GST reductions to consumers; and
(d) the findings of such studies and the steps taken to curb profiteering and ensure price reductions?
J

(a) the number and details of airports developed, revived or made operational under the UDAN scheme in each State/UT, along with the year of commencement of operations and the expenditure incurred;
(b) the details of airports that have ceased or temporarily discontinued flight operations, along with the State/UT, year of commencement, year of discontinuation and the reasons for cessation;
(c) the details of the expenditure incurred on those airports where flight operations have ceased or remain non-operational; and
(d) the number of passengers handled at each airport operationalised under the UDAN scheme, airport-wise and year-wise since commencement of operations?

(a) the total quantity and value of steel exported from and imported into the country during each of the last five years and the current year, year-wise;
(b) the country-wise details of major destinations for steel exports and major sources of steel imports during the said period;
(c) whether the country has become a net exporter or net importer of steel during the last five years, year-wise; and
(d) the details of new steel plants/industries established in the country during the last five years, indicating the State-wise location, production capacity and investment involved?

(a) the number of persons killed or injured in attacks by wild animals (including elephants, tigers, leopards and others) in each State and Union Territory, from 2019-20 to 2024-25, year-wise and State-wise;
(b) the details of ex-gratia/compensation provided by Central and State Governments in each of those years, State-wise; and
(c) the number of families/next-of-kin who received such compensation, year-wise and State-wise?

(a) the number of regular employees in Bharat Sanchar Nigam Limited (BSNL), during the last five years, year-wise;
(b) the number of employees who have taken voluntary retirement since 2021, year-wise;
(c) the number of persons presently working in BSNL on contract/outsourced basis, circle-wise and category-wise;
(d) whether Government is conducting regular recruitments to fill the vacancies arising due to retirements; and
(e) the details of recruitment notifications issued during the last five years, indicating the number of posts, category and status of filling up of such posts?

(a) the number of complaints received during the last five years relating to medical negligence, including cases of retained surgical instruments, sponges or other foreign objects left in patients’ bodies after surgery, in medical institutions under the Central Government, year-wise;
(b) the hospital-wise data with category-wise break-up of such complaints, including surgical negligence, diagnostic errors, medication errors, post-operative complications and other forms of alleged negligence; and
(c) the action taken on these complaints, including disciplinary proceedings against medical personnel, compensation awarded to patients, cases referred to the National Medical Commission or other authorities and the status thereof?

(a) the amount of haircut incurred under resolutions completed through the Insolvency and Bankruptcy Code (IBC) since its inception, year-wise;
(b) the total claims admitted vis-à-vis the amount realised by banks and financial institutions during this period;
(c) the effective loss borne by public sector banks due to such haircuts; and
(d) whether any assessment has been made on the long-term impact of IBC resolutions on the financial health of banks?

(a) the total proven and probable reserves of crude oil and natural gas in the country, basin-wise, as on date;
(b) the year-wise details of domestic crude oil and natural gas production during the last three years, along with the assessed production potential and the difference between potential and actual production, year-wise; and
(c) the reasons for the gap between reserves, assessed potential and actual production, and the steps being taken to enhance domestic output and reduce import dependence?

(a) the total funds allocated, released and utilised under major housing and urban development schemes, including Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana (Urban), AMRUT and Smart Cities Mission, during the last five years, year-wise and State-wise;
(b) the number of housing units and urban infrastructure projects sanctioned, completed and pending, along with reasons for delays, if any; and
(c) the steps being taken to address cost escalation, implementation bottlenecks, inter-State disparities and quality concerns, and to ensure timely delivery and inclusive urban development?

(a) the procedure, criteria and approvals followed for allotment of stalls/exhibition space at the India AI Impact Summit 2026 held in New Delhi;
(b) whether any technical or institutional mechanism existed to verify the claims made by exhibitors and whether misleading or false AI-related claims were displayed, if so, the details thereof along with the action taken;
(c) the total number of participating institutions, the details thereof, category-wise; and
(d) the total expenditure incurred by Government and Government institutions on the Summit, item-wise?

(a) the percentage of the total cost proposed to be borne by the Union Government under the Viksit Bharat-Guarantee for Rozgar and Ajeevika Mission (Gramin) (VB–G RAMG) Act;
(b) whether, in comparison to the MGNREG Act, the Union Government’s share as a percentage of total expenditure under the scheme will increase or decrease, the details thereof;
(c) the percentage share borne by the Union Government under the MGNREG Scheme during the last five years; and
(d) the percentage increase in the financial burden on State Governments under the VB–GRAMG scheme as compared to MGNREG?

(a) the total number of hospitals and health units functioning under Indian Railways for its employees and their dependents, zone-wise;
(b) the staffing pattern (doctors, nurses, paramedics, support staff) for these hospitals and the number of existing vacancies in each category;
(c) the number of complaints received in the last three years regarding medical negligence or deficiencies in hospital functioning, with details of action taken; and
(d) the steps taken to improve quality, reduce vacancies and strengthen railway health services?

(a) the number of senior artists, including traditional, folk, classical and performing artists, currently receiving pensions or financial support under various schemes of the Ministry;
(b) the eligibility criteria, quantum of pension and the duration for which such financial support is provided;
(c) whether the Ministry has received any requests or complaints regarding delay or inadequacy of pension payments to elderly artists; and
(d) the steps taken or proposed to ensure timely and adequate pension, social security and welfare support for senior and veteran artists, particularly those from rural areas or marginalized communities?
v

(a) the total emoluments (honorarium, incentives and other allowances) paid to scheme workers engaged under the Ministry, including Anganwadi Workers, Anganwadi Helpers, Mini-Anganwadi Workers and Supervisors, during the last three financial years and the current year, with a component-wise and State-wise/UT-wise details therof;
(b) the details of the last revision of their incentive/honorarium structure by the Union Government, specifying the date of revision, components revised and the rationale for the changes; and
(c) whether any further revision is under consideration to ensure living wages across States/UTs and if so, the timeline and expected impact on workers’ earnings?

(a) the year-wise and institution-wise details of funds allocated by Government for research and innovation in Higher Education Institutions, including Central Universities, IITs, NITs, IISERs and other centrally funded institutions, during the last five years and the current financial year;
(b) the discipline-wise breakup of such allocations, indicating major fields of research supported; and
(c) the extent of utilisation of these funds and whether any assessment has been made of the outcomes or impact of the research funded under the Ministry?

(a) the amount of funds allocated in the Union Budget for existing and for setting up of new AIIMS, during the last five years, year-wise and State-wise;
(b) the actual expenditure incurred against these allocations and the amount of funds, if any, that remained unutilised or lapsed, year-wise; and
(c) the steps taken to ensure timely utilisation of funds and completion of new AIIMS projects?

(a) the total collections of personal income tax and corporate tax for each of the last five financial years and the annual percentage growth in collections for both taxes during the said period, year-wise;
(b) the reasons for differences in growth rates between income tax and corporate tax collections, including any impact of tax policy changes such as revisions in corporate tax rates and income tax relief measures; and
(c) whether Government has any plan to increase corporate tax rates or reduce the income tax burden on individual taxpayers, if so, the details thereof?

(a) the total amount of funds allocated by the Central Government under the Smart Cities Mission (SCM) since its inception, year-wise;
(b) the amount of funds, if any, that have remained unutilised or lapsed under the Mission, year-wise, along with the reasons therefor;
(c) the total number of cities selected under the SCM and the names of such cities, State/UT-wise; and
(d) the number of Smart Cities in which projects have been fully completed, the number of cities where projects are near completion and the number of cities where projects are still pending?

(a) the number of blocks identified as over-exploited, critical and semi-critical in terms of groundwater extraction during the last five years, State-wise;
(b) the impact of Jal Shakti Abhiyan on groundwater recharge; and
(c) whether any independent assessment of long-term sustainability has been conducted?

(a) the percentage of rural households provided with functional household tap connections under the Jal Jeevan Mission, State-wise;
(b) the number of habitations still dependent on tanker water supply during the last three years; and
(c) the steps taken to ensure equitable access to safe drinking water for SC/ST, coastal, hilly and drought-prone regions?

(a) the present status of doubling and capacity enhancement works on the Kasaragod–Mangaluru, Shoranur–Ernakulam, and Ernakulam–Kayamkulam railway sections in Kerala;
(b) the section-wise timelines fixed for completion of these works, along with the year of sanction and original target dates;
(c) the reasons for delay, if any, in each of the above sections; and
(d) the steps taken or proposed to be taken to ensure time-bound completion of these projects, considering the severe congestion on Kerala’s railway network?
J

(a) the number of sanctioned posts, the number of posts filled on a permanent basis, the number of personnel engaged on contract and the number of vacancies in Indian embassies and consulates, country-wise and year-wise during the last five years;
(b) whether the existing staffing strength is adequate to handle consular services, grievance redressal and emergency assistance for Indian nationals abroad; and
(c) the steps taken or proposed to be taken to address staffing shortages and infrastructure constraints in Missions, particularly in countries with a large Indian diaspora?

(a) the total number of Professors of Practice appointed in Central Universities, Centrally funded educational institutions in the country during last five years, year-wise and institution-wise;
(b) the total number of Professors of Practice appointed in private Universities and State Universities, details thereof, year-wise; 
 (c) whether any reservation or affirmative action criteria (including SC, ST, OBC, EWS, PwDs, etc.) are applicable in such appointments and the details thereof; and
 (d) the number of persons appointed, including women, men and persons of other gender identities, as Professors of Practice during the said period, year-wise, gender-wise?

(a) whether Government is aware that patients and their attendants are forced to lie outside wards and OPD areas at AIIMS, New Delhi, even during extreme cold weather;
(b) whether any winter preparedness protocol exists for Central Government hospitals including AIIMS;
(c) the sanctioned bed strength at AIIMS, New Delhi vis-à-vis actual patient inflow during the last three years;
(d) the reasons for the acute shortage of beds and waiting space; and
(e) the immediate measures taken to provide shelter, heating and basic facilities to such patients?

(a) the airports in the country where User Development Fee (UDF) is being levied on passengers at present;
(b) the rate of UDF charged at each such airport, separately for domestic and international passengers;
(c) the name of the operating agency managing each such airport;
(d) the rates and total amount of user fee collected under UDF during each of the last five years, year-wise or revision-wise and airport-wise; and
(e) the factors taken into account while revising UDF?

(a) the total number of railway overbridges and underpasses (ROBs/ROUs) sanctioned in Kerala till date, along with the total estimated cost of these projects;
(b) the details of the funds and resources contributed by the Indian Railways and Government of Kerala in respect of each of these projects, project-wise;
(c) the number and names of projects where Indian Railways has borne 100 per cent of the cost owing to non-availability of Kerala’s share and the justification for such decisions; and
(d) the present status of implementation and timelines for completion of all such sanctioned ROB/ROU projects in Kerala, project-wise?

(a) the details of the National Overseas Scholarship awarded to students from Scheduled Castes, Denotified Nomadic and Semi-Nomadic Tribes, during the last five years, indicating the number of beneficiaries each year;
(b) the amount of scholarship granted each year, along with a State-wise/UT-wise and category-wise break-up, if so, the details thereof; and
(c) the steps taken or proposed to increase awareness, participation and timely disbursal of the scholarship to eligible students, ensuring greater access to higher education abroad for marginalized communities?

(a) the State-wise/UT-wise details of revenue devolved to Local Self Governments (LSGs), including panchayats and urban local bodies, during the last five years, specifying the amount transferred as well as the percentage of each State/UT total own revenue represented by such devolution annually;
(b) the criteria adopted by each State/UT Government for revenue sharing with LSGs, including whether these are based on recommendations of the State Finance Commission or any other statutory mechanism; and
(c) whether Government has assessed inter-State/UT variations in the proportion of revenue devolved to LSGs and if so, the findings and steps taken to address the issue?

(a) the year-wise funds allocated under the Namami Gange Programme during the last five years;
(b) the amount actually spent and the funds remaining unutilised, year-wise, during the said period; and
(c) the component-wise details of expenditure incurred on sewage treatment infrastructure, river surface cleaning, rural sanitation, afforestation, biodiversity conservation, public awareness and administrative expenses under the programme during the last five years?

(a) whether it is a fact that the final investigation report of the aircraft crash that occurred in the State of Gujarat in June, 2025 has not yet been made public, even after several months of the incident;
(b) whether a preliminary report was issued and, if so, the key findings emerging from it;
(c) the specific reasons for the delay in publishing the final report;
(d) whether any interim safety advisories or corrective measures have been issued to airlines based on preliminary findings and if so, the details thereof; and
(e) the definite timeline by when the final report will be placed in the public domain?

(a) the number of Indian workers who died abroad during the last five years, year-wise and country-wise;
(b) whether Government is cognizant about the exploitation and injustice faced by the Indian workers and if so, the details of complaints or abuse, year-wise and country-wise;
(c) whether India has protested against exploitative labour practices faced by Indian workers in foreign countries, in the Gulf, Europe and North America; and
(d) if so, the details thereof and the measures taken by Government to raise the concerns on appropriate fora?

(a) the number of environmental, forest and CRZ clearances granted for projects in the Andaman and Nicobar Islands during the last five years, project-wise and year-wise;
(b) the details thereof including the name of project, project proponent, extent of land diverted (in hectares), forest area involved, number of trees proposed to be cut down and clearance conditions imposed; and
(c) whether any comprehensive, independent assessment has been carried out to evaluate the cumulative ecological damage caused by these projects to forests, mangroves, coral reefs, wildlife habitats and livelihood of indigenous and local communities and if so, the findings thereof?

(a) the State-wise, year-wise number of crimes reported on railway premises and onboard trains during the last five years, including theft, robbery, assault, sexual offences, vandalism and other offences recorded by RPF/GRP;
(b) the number of persons injured or affected in these incidents, year-wise; and
(c) the total amount of compensation provided to victims during this period year-wise and State-wise?

(a) the number of Indian nationals detained abroad as illegal immigrants and the number of Indians deported from foreign countries during the last five years, country-wise and year-wise;
(b) whether Government has examined the reasons for such detentions and deportations, including irregular migration and visa violations; and
(c) the measures taken to curb fraudulent agents, strengthen safe migration systems and ensure legal assistance and timely repatriation for affected Indian nationals?

(a) the year-wise details of financial, skill-development and livelihood assistance provided during the last five years by the National Scheduled Castes Finance and Development Corporation (NSFDC), the National Safai Karamcharis Finance and Development Corporation (NSKFDC) and the National Backward Classes Finance and Development Corporation (NBCFDC);
(b) the year-wise amount spent by each of these corporations during the last five years; and
(c) the number of beneficiaries assisted under their major schemes, State-wise and year-wise?

(a) the debt of the Union Government, Internal and External, year-wise for the last five years;
(b) the Debt-to-GDP Ratio of the Union Government, year-wise during the last five years;
(c) the amount spent on servicing of debt, year-wise during the last five years;
